Vendored node-type icon set
===========================

Source:  Material Design Icons (MDI), the Pictogrammers community set, distributed
         as the npm package `@mdi/svg` (https://github.com/Templarian/MaterialDesign-SVG).
License: Apache License 2.0.
Vendored: 2026-07-15, fetched from https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@mdi/svg/svg/<name>.svg

These are permissive, engine- and cloud-agnostic glyphs. There are deliberately NO AWS / Azure /
GCP brand/architecture icons here (those carry trademark + redistribution caveats — see
node-type-icons.md §5). Every icon is a LOCAL file, referenced by relative path only; nothing is
fetched at render time (a remote icon would break air-gap and silently render broken).

Each file is named by its node-type token (node-type-icons.json). Type -> MDI source name:

  service.svg        <- mdi:server
  process.svg        <- mdi:cog
  datastore.svg      <- mdi:database
  queue.svg          <- mdi:tray-full
  external-actor.svg <- mdi:account
  external-dep.svg   <- mdi:package-variant
  identity.svg       <- mdi:account-key
  secret.svg         <- mdi:key
  control.svg        <- mdi:shield-check
  pipeline.svg       <- mdi:pipe
  trust-boundary.svg <- mdi:fence
  gateway.svg        <- mdi:call-split
  neutral.svg        <- mdi:shape
  unknown.svg        <- mdi:help-circle
  other.svg          <- mdi:dots-horizontal

